## One Codebase, Three Platforms

```xiom
// Conditional compilation
#[cfg(target_os = "linux")]
fn get_home_dir() -> Str { return os.get_env("HOME"); }

#[cfg(target_os = "macos")]
fn get_home_dir() -> Str { return os.get_env("HOME"); }

#[cfg(target_os = "windows")]
fn get_home_dir() -> Str { return os.get_env("USERPROFILE"); }

fn main() {
  let home = get_home_dir();
  io.println("Home: " + home);
}
```

### Platform Conditional Compilation

```xiom
#[cfg(target_os = "linux")]
const LINE_ENDING: Str = "\n";

#[cfg(target_os = "windows")]
const LINE_ENDING: Str = "\r\n";

#[cfg(any(target_os = "linux", target_os = "macos"))]
fn use_unix_api() { /* POSIX-specific code */ }
```

### Cross-Compilation

```sh
# Build for Linux from macOS
xiom build --target x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu

# Build for Windows from Linux
xiom build --target x86_64-pc-windows-msvc

# Build for macOS from Linux
xiom build --target x86_64-apple-darwin
```

### Platform Abstraction Layer

```xiom
pub interface FileSystem {
  fn read(path: &Str) -> Result[Str, Error];
  fn write(path: &Str, data: &Str) -> Result[(), Error];
  fn exists(path: &Str) -> Bool;
  fn home_dir() -> Str;
}

// Each platform implements FileSystem
#[cfg(target_os = "linux")]
pub type NativeFS = LinuxFS;

#[cfg(target_os = "windows")]
pub type NativeFS = WindowsFS;
```

### Platform Matrix Testing

```yaml
# Test on all platforms
strategy:
  matrix:
    os: [ubuntu-latest, macos-latest, windows-latest]
```

### Common Cross-Platform Issues

- **Path separators**: `/` on Unix, `\` on Windows
- **Line endings**: `\n` on Unix, `\r\n` on Windows
- **Case sensitivity**: Unix filesystem is case-sensitive, Windows is not
- **API differences**: POSIX on Unix, Win32 on Windows
- **Available tools**: curl on Unix, Invoke-WebRequest on Windows

